  "notes": "This feature is an exposure/behavior extension of existing interfaces, so the inventory is the honest delta surface: the worker entry capability, the one new field (scriptCount, also flag-added on main-thread entries), and the PerformanceScriptTiming worker exposure delta. Existing main-thread members (renderStart, blockingDuration, scripts, etc.) are documented by MDN and the LoAF spec; this reference documents only how their meaning changes in worker entries (worker-entries/#return-value). The LoAF spec has no worker text yet (Intent to Prototype: 'Specification: No information provided'), so worker behavior is transcribed from the Chromium implementation and its WPT suite with the prototype status stated prominently. The explainer's cadence, executionContext, PerformanceExecutionContextInfo, OffscreenCanvas frame cadence, and configurable durationThreshold are proposed but NOT implemented as of 2026-09-13 and are documented as such, not inventoried as available surface."
